    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into favorable matchups against soft-tossing rotations, with **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.72) anchoring our offensive production. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a premium spot in the order and a soft matchup against Quintana, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains a strong score despite the 1.86s pop time risk from the opposing catcher, as his elite profile against Painter remains the core engine of our lineup. **Daulton Varsho** (67.26) and **Taylor Ward** (66.35) are also high-confidence starts; both benefit significantly from park factors and platoon advantages, with **Daulton Varsho** specifically positioned to capitalize on a favorable RHP matchup. While we are prioritizing efficiency to manage our game caps, the combination of **Taylor Ward** at the top of the order and **Daulton Varsho** in a productive slot creates high-ceiling opportunities for R and RBI production.\n\nThe decision to bench **Lawrence Butler** was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Lawrence Butler** (projected at 55.27 if starting) possesses the power profile we covet, he currently lacks an confirmed path into the lineup; with **Gavin Sheets** (53.42) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (52.61) providing acceptable floor production in active slots, we cannot justify burning an active roster spot on uncertainty. We remain concerned about **Bryson Stott** (40.48), whose score is suppressed by a difficult encounter with Messick; he remains in the lineup only because of his defensive versatility, but he is a candidate for an early pull if his efficiency continues to slide. Elsewhere, **Jonathan Aranda** (46.56) and **Matt Chapman** (55.56) face meaningful hurdles against Weathers and Schultz, respectively. We are keeping a close watch on **Jeremiah Jackson**; while his batting order spot is suboptimal, his sprint speed provides the essential stolen base upside we prioritize in our 5x5 build, making him a necessary inclusion even as he faces a tough arm in Valdez.",
